A||N||8||Trixi||Tach surge||||8||
Z||000000||Trixi||02-14-2000||02:54 PM||||I have an 84 and I resently had a new tranny put in her.  I've had her laid up for a month, due to winter weather.  Now when you're going about 100 kmph the tach will surge from 3 to 6 grand, without the motor revving up (it does this five or six times, then stops). <P>Also when I come to a stop she idles down and almost stalls. <P>The volts gauge goes from the middle (13) down to the bottom (11).  <P>What's wrong? <BR>Help!||||reg||8
Z||000001||ka4nkf||02-14-2000||03:14 PM||||It sounds like you have a bad tach filter. this will make it run bad and tach jump around. I know where the tach filter is located on the V6 but i dont know on the four cyl. Maybe some one else will respond.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-14-2000||06:43 PM||||I think it's on a bolt next to the thermostat shell on the 4. ((My 87 doesn't use one. That's where I rememeber seeing it in the scrap yard last I looked.))||||reg||1
Z||000003||wkayl||02-15-2000||12:40 AM||||ka4nkf<BR>Where is the filter located on the v-6?  My son's GT does this also.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||02-15-2000||01:41 PM||||wkayl The Filter on the V6 is located right under the coil. it is a round can looks like a condensor with wire connector. you can test it by unpluging it and if you motor runs ok then this is the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Trixi||02-16-2000||12:08 PM||||Well so far the problem seems to be just the fact that the starter was faulty.  We had it rebuild and it works fine, the tach or voltmeter doesn't jump! <P>Thanks!||||reg||10
Z||000006||Rodrv6||02-16-2000||04:13 PM||||Trixi, <BR>If you ever have the same problem in the future, don't have the starter rebuilt!  Your problem was the connection on the starter where the battery cable hooks up to it.  On the 84 models only, there are two other wires that also attatch to the same large stud.  These are the fusible links that carry power to the rest of the car.  If the nut that secures these wires onto the starter works loose even a little, or gets corrosion on it, then you will have the same symptoms you described.  Usually the nut just needs to be re-tightened.  I have an 84--been there, done that!||||reg||10
Z||000007||Trixi||02-16-2000||05:26 PM||||Rodrv6<BR>It needed starter rebuild anyway!<BR>It was getting really hard to start, then just wouldn't!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||02-16-2000||05:34 PM||||I had a similiar problem with my V6.  I replaced the tach filter, no fix.  It turned out to be a loose battery connection.  The most simple things really screw you up.||||reg||1
